{
  "dom_id": "step-q131946",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "To make a fruit sponge, Dimo mixes $3$ pounds of cherries with $2$ pounds of raisins. What ratio describes the amount of cherries to the amount of raisins?",
  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the amount of cherry to the amount of raisins as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of cherry}:\\text{amount of raisins}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of cherries. There are $3$ pounds of cherries.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of raisins. There are $2$ pounds of raisins.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of cherries to raisins is $3:2.$",
